// REJECTS: Unsupported SecurityScheme - OAuth
//
// `security: [ OAuth ]`. The field is REQUIRED on every Service (ServiceStoreParseTreeWalker
// :204) and the grammar accepts a comma-separated list of scheme islands -- but nothing in
// legend-engine implements IServiceStoreGrammarParserExtension.getExtraSecuritySchemesParsers(),
// so the lookup at :380 fails for EVERY name a user could write. `security: []` is the only
// spelling that reaches the token, which is why ../fixtures/t2-servicestore.pure writes the
// empty list twice and never a scheme.
//
// A required list that must always be empty is not a thing a grammar can express, so this is
// invisible to anyone transcribing the .g4: they get a working `security: [ Basic ]` for free
// and a store that upstream refuses. Same category as ./no-registered-island-processor.pure
// (HostedService `actions`) and ./no-registered-persistence-strategy.pure -- island types
// with zero registered processors -- but this one fails with a NAMED message rather than a
// crash, and the name is what distinguishes "no processor registered" from "extension missing
// from the classpath".
###ServiceStore
ServiceStore fixture::neg::SecuredStore
(
  Service GetEmployee
  (
    path: '/employees';
    method: GET;
    response: fixture::neg::Employee <- fixture::neg::Binding;
    security: [ OAuth ];
  )
)
